# Forecast engine

Location: app/server/services/forecast/*

Core modules (selected)
- ForecastEngine — orchestrator for a single run
- DataLoaderService — loads DB state into in-memory/cache structures
- AccountRegisterService — account-level operations and projections
- ReoccurrenceService — schedule generation and amount adjustments
- RegisterEntryService — materializes ledger entries
- LoanCalculatorService — interest and amortization
- TransferService — inter-register transfers with validation and ordering
- DateTime/DateTimeService — date math, weekend adjustments, intervals
- ModernCacheService — optimized in-memory caching
- DataPersisterService — persists snapshots/results back to DB
- getProjectedBalanceAtDate.ts — helper for point-in-time projection

## Skipped occurrences

- `ReoccurrenceSkip` rows are the source of truth for skipping a specific instance date.
- DataLoader loads skips into cache (`skippedAt` as `YYYY-MM-DD`).
- `ReoccurrenceService` must omit skipped dates when creating entries/transfers (check adjusted and nominal dates); still advance the schedule so later occurrences generate.
- `ForecastEngine` also filters skipped entries before running balances / persist (safety net).
- Do **not** rely on bumping `lastAt` alone to persist a skip — future skips survive only via skip rows (and `persistReoccurrenceLastAt` does not walk `lastAt` into the future).
- Skip API (`register-entry-skip`) always inserts a skip row; may also bump `lastAt` when skipping the immediate next occurrence using `calculateNextOccurrenceDate` (same math as forecast).
- Edit modal: a today/future **projected** recurrence shows **Skip this occurrence** only (not Apply). Apply/Clear/Delete are for posted or past pending rows — Apply posts the instance; Skip means it will not happen.
- Register description origin icon: projected recurrences use **repeat**; once the occurrence date has passed or the row has a Plaid match (`plaidId` / `isMatched`), swap to **badge-check**. Manual / transfer / interest / bank-import rows use other icons (`registerEntryOrigin.ts`).

## Balances (do not overwrite live snapshot)

- DataLoader maps DB `latestBalance` into cache `balance` **and** `latestBalance` for projections.
- ForecastEngine must **not** call `updateAccountRegisterBalances` / write `latest_balance` after a run — Plaid/user edits are the source of truth for the live snapshot.
- Persister may still update entry running `balance` columns and pocket auto-apply increments.
- Agent rule: `.cursor/rules/register-balances.mdc`.

## Money rounding

- Entry amounts are normalized to whole cents via bankers rounding (`roundToCents` from `~/lib/bankers-rounding`) inside `RegisterEntryService.createEntry`.
- Reoccurrence amount adjustments and percent splits also use bankers rounding (not `Math.round` half-up).
- Running-balance accumulation in `lib/sort.ts` is left as float sum of already-rounded amounts.
- Agent rule: `.cursor/rules/forecast-money-rounding.mdc`.

## Month-end schedule anchors

- Monthly/yearly reoccurrences preserve day-of-month via `Reoccurrence.scheduleAnchorAt` (preferred day clamped to each month’s length: Jan 31 → Feb 28/29 → Mar 31).
- When `scheduleAnchorAt` is null, EOM-sticky applies: if `lastAt` is the last day of its month, target day 31 (end of next months).
- Upsert/create sets `scheduleAnchorAt` from `lastAt`; clone copies it. Migration should backfill `schedule_anchor_at = last_at`.

## Loan interest and payments

- Interest posts first; payment amount is capped against the **post-interest** projected balance.
- If `targetAccountRegisterId` is null, post interest only — never invent a single-sided payment (no phantom net-worth gain).

## Transfers

- Skip self-transfers (`source === target`) and transfers involving archived registers.

## Unused schema fields

- `Reoccurrence.totalIntervals` / `elapsedIntervals` are cloned and stored but **not read** by the forecast engine. Do not treat them as an occurrence cap until a product write path exists.

## Depreciation

- Declining-balance and compound depreciation both floor at `assetResidualValue` for depreciating assets.

Testing
- Extensive unit/integration/regression tests under app/server/services/forecast/__tests__
- Calculation regressions: `calculation-bugs.regression.test.ts`, `multiYearLedger.golden.test.ts`
- Agents: do not add/run tests unless the user asks (see `.cursor/rules/05-workflow-execution.mdc`)

Guidance
- Keep deterministic results under known seeds; avoid relying on wall clock outside DateTimeService
- Rate limits and performance tunings in forecast/lib/rateLimiter.ts — consider when expanding scope
